---
---

<section class="border-t border-(--color-border-soft) bg-(--color-surface)/40 py-24">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">
    <div class="grid gap-14 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center">
      <div>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs tracking-widest text-(--color-accent-dim) uppercase">
          Architecture differentiator
        </p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-(--color-ink) sm:text-4xl">
          Firehose ingestion, not query-per-domain.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-(--color-ink-muted)">
          Watching lookalikes at scale means watching permutations, not just
          domains: 20 real domains fed through <code
            class="rounded bg-(--color-surface-2) px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[13px] text-(--color-ink)"
            >dnstwist</code
          > becomes roughly <strong class="text-(--color-ink)">100,000</strong> lookalike
          variants to monitor. A query-per-domain API model needs 100,000
          requests to sweep that set once. Merkleye doesn't query at all —
          it subscribes to the unfiltered CT firehose through a self-hosted <code
            class="rounded bg-(--color-surface-2) px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[13px] text-(--color-ink)"
            >certstream</code
          > sidecar, and every certificate on the stream reaches the matcher.
          Nothing is filtered upstream, so there is no watchlist to outgrow —
          which is what makes watching six figures of variants
          architecturally tractable instead of a rate-limit problem. <code
            class="rounded bg-(--color-surface-2) px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[13px] text-(--color-ink)"
            >certspotter</code
          > ships alongside it as the lighter, pre-filtered path.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-(--color-ink-muted)">
          Global CT issuance runs roughly <strong class="text-(--color-ink)"
            >20–30 million entries a day</strong
          >. Merkleye discards everything that doesn't match — only matches
          are persisted, so your storage footprint tracks your hit rate, not
          the internet's issuance volume.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div
        class="rounded-xl border border-(--color-border) bg-(--color-surface) p-6 sm:p-8"
      >
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between font-mono text-xs text-(--color-ink-faint)">
          <span>query-per-domain</span>
          <span>firehose (Merkleye)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 gap-5">
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-(--color-border-soft) bg-(--color-surface-2) p-5">
            <div class="font-mono text-3xl font-semibold text-(--color-danger)">100,000</div>
            <div class="mt-1 text-xs text-(--color-ink-faint)">API requests per sweep</div>
            <div class="mt-4 h-2 w-full rounded-full bg-(--color-border-soft)">
              <div class="h-2 w-full rounded-full bg-(--color-danger)/70"></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-(--color-accent-dim) bg-(--color-accent)/10 p-5">
            <div class="font-mono text-3xl font-semibold text-(--color-accent)">1</div>
            <div class="mt-1 text-xs text-(--color-ink-faint)">continuous log stream</div>
            <div class="mt-4 h-2 w-full rounded-full bg-(--color-border-soft)">
              <div class="h-2 w-[3%] rounded-full bg-(--color-accent)"></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-6 rounded-lg border border-(--color-border-soft) bg-(--color-surface-2)/60 p-5">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-sm">
            <span class="text-(--color-ink-muted)">CT issuance, global</span>
            <span class="font-mono text-(--color-ink)">~20–30M / day</span>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-3 flex items-center justify-between text-sm">
            <span class="text-(--color-ink-muted)">Stored by Merkleye</span>
            <span class="font-mono text-(--color-accent-dim)">matches only</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
